      "candidate": "**Repaired Scraper Code**\n\n```python\n# corrected_scraper.py\nimport re\nimport requests\nfrom bs4 import BeautifulSoup\n\ndef scrape_gpu(url: str):\n    \"\"\"Scrapes a GPU product page and returns data in gpu-price-schema-v1 format.\"\"\"\n    response = requests.get(url, timeout=10)\n    soup = BeautifulSoup(response.text, \"html.parser\")\n\n    product = {\n        \"product_id\": url.rstrip(\"/\").split(\"/\")[-1],\n        \"title\": soup.select_one(\"h1.product-title\").get_text(strip=True),\n        \"price\": float(\n            re.sub(r\"[^\\d.]\", \"\", soup.select_one(\"span.price\").get_text())\n        ),\n        \"availability\": \"in_stock\" if soup.select_one(\".in-stock\") else \"out_of_stock\",\n        \"rating\": float(\n            soup.select_one(\"div.rating\").get_text(strip=True)\n        ),\n        \"url\": url,\n    }\n\n    # Convert the internal mappingproxy to a plain dict for serialization\n    return dict(product)\n```\n\n**Change Made**  \nThe original scraper returned a `mappingproxy` object, which is not JSON\u2011serializable and conflicts with the `gpu-price-schema-v1` expectations. The revised code copies the mapping into a standard Python `dict` before returning, ensuring the output matches the required schema."
